// A defer INSIDE a seal.
//
// The order is the whole claim: a user `defer` declared inside the region must
// run BEFORE `sys_seal_exit`, because its body is cleanup that may still touch
// the protected registers. It falls out of the chain being LIFO — the desugar
// registers the seam exit FIRST, so it runs LAST — but "falls out of" is a
// hypothesis until the trace says so.
fn f() {
    seal {
        println(1);
        defer { println(3); }   // cleanup, still inside the region
        println(2);
    }
    println(4);                 // the region is closed by here
}
fn main() { f(); }
